  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ILAC core support 2018-2021 - ILAC core support 2018-2020</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ILAC k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d 2018-2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Core support to ILAC - a network of fifty organisations working on rehabilitation of justice systems in and after conflict. ILAC is running Sida-funded programs and this core support allows ILAC to remain flexible and apt to resopnd to needs for, amongst others, country specific analyses of justice systems and to formulate recommendations for national and international actors to align with. ILAC also works to influence on policy development in the area of justice systems in conflict-affected countries. 
Sida includes, in the core support, funding for a specific exchange exercise between Tunisian and Palestinian representatives for the justice systems on management of tensions between secular and islamist groups and standpoints.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">K&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d till International Legal Assistance Consortium (ILAC) - en n&#xe4;tverksorganisation, med sekretariat i Sverige, f&#xf6;r sammanslutningar av professioner inom r&#xe4;ttsomr&#xe5;det p&#xe5; nationell eller internationell niv&#xe5;. ILAC arbetar f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;rebyggande av &#xe5;terfall i konflikt genom st&#xf6;d till &#xe5;teruppbyggnad av oberoende r&#xe4;ttssystem och samh&#xe4;llen byggda p&#xe5; r&#xe4;ttsstatens principer. St&#xf6;det inneb&#xe4;r k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d till ILAC, som ocks&#xe5; bedriver program finansierade av andra Sidaenheter respektive utlandsmyndigheter. K&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;det ger ILAC flexibilitet och m&#xf6;jlighet att svara upp mot behov och efterfr&#xe5;gan p&#xe5; bland annat f&#xf6;rdjupade analyser av r&#xe4;ttsystem i konflikt eller post-konfliktskeden samt att p&#xe5;verka och bidra till policyutveckling inom st&#xf6;d till r&#xe4;ttsstatsuppbyggnad i konfliktkontexter. I st&#xf6;det omfattas ocks&#xe5; medel f&#xf6;r ett specifikt utbytesprojekt mellan tunisiska och palestinska akt&#xf6;rer inom r&#xe4;ttsv&#xe4;sendena f&#xf6;r att m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;ra delande av erfarenheter fr&#xe5;n den tunisiska reformprocessen med de palestinska akt&#xf6;rerna.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILAC Strategic Plan for 2017-2021 contains three objectives:

1. The capacity of justice sector institutions, bar associations and their members to address public demands for accountability and justice in accordance with international standards, is enhanced.

2. International policy and practice in rule of law reform has been influenced.

3. Internal ILAC systems and capacities for demand-driven, flexible and coherent operations are further developed, and synergies within the membership to better capitalise on cutting-edge expertise are improved.</narrative>
  </description>
